  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "HAU2Z1JyC6EWUeBm87bK76JlSqQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:23:49.383Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "n8n keeps no ordered business record. Its execution data is prunable, and pruning is on by default \u2014 so the history of what the automation did is a retention-managed cache, not a log. Nothing has to be misconfigured for the record to vanish; the default configuration is the failure mode.\n\nThe resulting position is straightforward: Powerhouse is the durable log the automation writes to as it runs. The workflow keeps doing what it does well \u2014 triggering, branching, calling APIs \u2014 and each business-relevant branch also emits an attributed, append-only entry that outlives the execution row. There is no contest over ownership of the automation layer.\n\nThis is the cleanest instance in the corpus of the general finding that open-source business tools do not keep an immutable attributed log by default. Most tools in the survey leave a mutable record; n8n's default actively deletes one. For the seven German integrators carrying this finding, that makes the gap demonstrable in the client's own installation rather than argued from documentation.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (7)\n\n**1 \u00b7 start here**\n- ETES GmbH (DE Stuttgart) \u2014 Markus Espenhain, Gesch\u00e4ftsf\u00fchrer \u00b7 info@etes.de \u00b7 https://etes.de\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Exxeta AG (DE Karlsruhe) \u2014 https://exxeta.com\n- Lighthouse Consultings (DE Stuttgart) \u2014 https://lighthouseconsultings.de\n- SVA System Vertrieb Alexander GmbH (DE Wiesbaden +29) \u2014 https://sva.de\n- bitbetter GmbH (DE Hamburg) \u2014 https://bitbetter.de\n- cimt ag (DE Hamburg + Berlin) \u2014 https://cimt-ag.de\n- relyon AG (wemakefuture) (DE (HQ unverified)) \u2014 https://wemakefuture.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> n8n keeps no ordered business record \u2014 execution data is prunable and pruning is on by default. Powerhouse is the durable log the automation writes to as it runs.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:23:49.383699Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:23:49.383703Z"
    }
  },
